2	PHP Coding Language Summary	1	content2.html	/content2.html	<h2>A summary of the PHP coding language</h2><br><br>PHP (Hypertext Preprocessor) is a server-side scripting language primarily used for web development. It runs on a web server and generates dynamic content that is sent to a user’s browser, usually in the form of HTML. Because the code executes on the server, users cannot see the PHP source code, which helps improve security. PHP is commonly embedded directly into HTML, making it easy to mix logic and presentation when building web pages.<br><br>One of PHP’s main strengths is its ability to create dynamic and interactive websites. It is often used to process form data, manage user authentication, handle sessions and cookies, and interact with databases. PHP works especially well with databases such as MySQL, allowing developers to store, retrieve, and update data efficiently. This makes it suitable for applications like blogs, online stores, and content management systems.<br><br>PHP is known for being relatively easy to learn. Its syntax is straightforward and shares similarities with languages like C and Java. PHP supports variables, control structures, functions, and object-oriented programming. It also includes built-in tools and libraries that simplify common web development tasks.<br><br>The language is open source and supported by a large global community. Many popular platforms such as WordPress, Laravel, and Symfony are built with PHP. Modern versions improved performance, security, and code quality, keeping PHP a strong choice for server-side development.<br><br><h3>Example of PHP code</h3><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"><?php include 'includes/vars.inc'; ?></textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"><?php include 'includes/header.inc'; ?></textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"><?php $PAGETITLE='MD Wiki Homepage'; ?></textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"><?php include 'includes/navbar.inc'; ?></textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"><img class="imgright" src="<?php echo $imgVAR; ?>md_poster.png" alt="Uh oh broken"></textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"><?php include 'includes/footer.inc'; ?></textarea>	0	01/09/2026	01/27/2026	1
3	JavaScript Coding Language Summary	1	content3.html	/content3.html	<h2>A summary of the Javascript coding language</h2><br><br>JavaScript makes websites interactive, working with HTML and CSS. It runs in the browser using the &lt;script&gt; tag. JavaScript uses variables, data types, functions, loops, and conditions to create logic. It interacts with the Document Object Model (DOM) to update page content in real time and responds to user events like clicks and typing.<br><br><h3>Example</h3><p id="message">Press a button.</p><button onclick="changeText()">Change Text</button><button onclick="showTime()">Show Time</button><script>function changeText(){document.getElementById("message").innerHTML="JavaScript changed this!";}function showTime(){document.getElementById("message").innerHTML=new Date().toLocaleTimeString();}</script>	0	02/03/2026	02/03/2026	1
