14	JavaScript Assignment	1	content14.html	/content14.html	<h2>Javascript "Assignment" tutorial</h2><br><br>This page teaches how JavaScript assignment operators work and how they change variable values.<br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="30" cols="70">[input]<p id="ASSIGNMENTS"></p><script>let x=67;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS").innerHTML="Value of x is: "+x;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS2"></p><script>let y=50;let x2=17+y;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS2").innerHTML=x2;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS3"></p><script>let a=10;a+=57;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS3").innerHTML=a;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS4"></p><script>let b=10;b-=5;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS4").innerHTML="Value of x is: "+b;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS5"></p><script>let c=10;c*=5;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS5").innerHTML="Value of x is: "+c;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS6"></p><script>let d=10;d**=5;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS6").innerHTML="Value of x is: "+d;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS7"></p><script>let e=135;e%=68;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS7").innerHTML="Value of x is: "+e;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS8"></p><script>let str="67";let str2=" Hello";document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS8").innerHTML=str+str2;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS9"></p><script>let text="I like ";text+="JavaScript";document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS9").innerHTML=text;</script><h2>Logical AND Assignment (&&=)</h2><p id="ASSIGNMENTS10"></p><script>let f=true;f&&=10;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS10").innerHTML=f;</script><h2>Logical OR Assignment (||=)</h2><p id="ASSIGNMENTS11"></p><script>let g=false;g||=10;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS11").innerHTML=g;</script><h2>Nullish Coalescing Assignment (??=)</h2><p id="ASSIGNMENTS12"></p><script>let h;h??=10;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS12").innerHTML=h;</script><p id="ASSIGNMENTS13"></p><script>let numbers="12345";let min=Math.min(...numbers);let max=Math.max(...numbers);document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS13").innerHTML="Min: "+min+" Max: "+max;</script>[/input]</textarea><h2>Examples</h2><p id="ASSIGNMENTS_EX"></p><script>let ex=67;document.getElementById("ASSIGNMENTS_EX").innerHTML=ex;</script>	0	02/04/2026	02/04/2026	1
15	JavaScript Data Types	1	content15.html	/content15.html	<h2>Javascript "Data Types" tutorial</h2><br><br>This page teaches JavaScript data types including String, Number, BigInt, Boolean, Object, Undefined, Null, and Symbol.<br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="30" cols="70">[input]<h2>Data Types Examples</h2><p id="DATATYPES"></p><script>let mix1=16+" Pontiac";document.getElementById("DATATYPES").innerHTML=mix1;</script><p id="DATATYPES2"></p><script>let mix2="Pontiac "+67;document.getElementById("DATATYPES2").innerHTML=mix2;</script><p id="DATATYPES3"></p><script>let mix3=63+4+" Pontiac";document.getElementById("DATATYPES3").innerHTML=mix3;</script><p id="DATATYPES4"></p><script>let mix4="Pontiac "+6+7;document.getElementById("DATATYPES4").innerHTML=mix4;</script><p id="DATATYPES5"></p><script>let dyn;dyn=67;dyn="Aloysius";document.getElementById("DATATYPES5").innerHTML=dyn;</script><p id="DATATYPES6"></p><script>let car1="Pontiac GTO";let car2='Pontiac GTO';document.getElementById("DATATYPES6").innerHTML=car1+"<br>"+car2;</script><p id="DATATYPES7"></p><script>let a1="It's alright";let a2="He is called 'Aloysius'";let a3='He is called "Aloysius"';document.getElementById("DATATYPES7").innerHTML=a1+"<br>"+a2+"<br>"+a3;</script><p id="DATATYPES8"></p><script>let n1=67.00,n2=67,n3=6.7,n4=0.67;document.getElementById("DATATYPES8").innerHTML=n1+"<br>"+n2+"<br>"+n3+"<br>"+n4;</script><p id="DATATYPES9"></p><script>let sci1=67e5,sci2=67e-5;document.getElementById("DATATYPES9").innerHTML=sci1+"<br>"+sci2;</script><p id="DATATYPES10"></p><script>let big=BigInt("123456789012345678901234567890");document.getElementById("DATATYPES10").innerHTML=big;</script><p id="DATATYPES11"></p><script>let b1=67,b2=67,b3=0.67;document.getElementById("DATATYPES11").innerHTML=(b1==b2)+"<br>"+(b1==b3);</script>[/input]</textarea><h2>Examples</h2><p id="DATATYPES_EX"></p><script>let ex="Yellow";document.getElementById("DATATYPES_EX").innerHTML=ex;</script>	0	02/04/2026	02/04/2026	1
16	Python Coding Language Summary	2	content16.html	/content16.html	<h2>A summary of the Python Coding language</h2><br><br>The Python tutorial starts with the fundamentals, introducing what Python is and how to write simple programs. It teaches basic syntax through easy examples like printing text, using comments, and running code step by step in an interactive editor. Early lessons focus on core building blocks such as variables, data types (strings, numbers, booleans), and basic operators, helping learners understand how information is stored and manipulated in a program.<br><br>As the tutorial continues, it moves into essential programming concepts that control how programs behave. These include conditional statements (if, elif, else) for decision-making and loops (for, while) for repeating actions. Learners are introduced to functions, which organize code into reusable sections, and common data structures like lists, tuples, sets, and dictionaries. These topics show how to manage collections of data and write more organized, efficient programs.<br><br>Later sections cover more practical and advanced uses of Python. This includes working with files (reading and writing data), handling errors with exceptions, and using modules to extend Python�s capabilities. There are also references for built-in methods and features, plus exercises and examples that reinforce learning through practice. Overall, the tutorial is designed to build a strong foundation in Python by combining explanations, working code examples, and hands-on experimentation.<br><br><h3>Example of Python code</h3><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30">name = "Aloysius"age = 17print("Hello,", name)print("You are", age, "years old.")</textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30">temperature = 75if temperature > 80:    print("It's hot outside!")elif temperature > 60:    print("Nice weather!")else:    print("It's cold!")</textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30">for i in range(5):    print("Number:", i)count = 1while count <= 3:    print("Count is", count)    count  = 1</textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30">fruits = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]for fruit in fruits:    print(fruit)student = {"name": "Aloysius", "grade": "A"}print(student["name"])print(student["grade"])</textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30">def greet(name):    return "Hello "   namemessage = greet("Aloysius")print(message)</textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30"># Write to a filewith open("example.txt", "w") as file:    file.write("Python is awesome!")# Read from a filewith open("example.txt", "r") as file:    content = file.read()    print(content)</textarea><br><br><textarea id="textbox" name="textbox" rows="5" cols="30">try:    number = int(input("Enter a number: "))    print(10 / number)except ZeroDivisionError:    print("You can't divide by zero!")except ValueError:    print("That was not a valid number.")</textarea>	0	02/05/2026	02/05/2026	1
